{"candidates":[{"checker_specs":[],"claim":"A panel of non-experts using a checklist is more reliable than a single expert for verifiable tasks because the checklist decomposes complex intuitive leaps into a series of low-variance binary checks, reducing the 'expert blind spot' of premature closure.","counterconditions":["The checklist is a lossy compression that omits a critical variable known only to the expert.","The non-experts possess a systematic bias that causes them to misinterpret a checklist item consistently."],"evidence_refs":[],"mechanism":"The checklist acts as a cognitive constraint that forces the processing of all known critical variables, preventing the expert's heuristic-driven 'leap' to a conclusion that may overlook a rare but verifiable outlier. Reliability is gained through the summation of these binary checks across multiple observers, which cancels out individual stochastic errors.","optional_refs":["280e2294b3011afadb10449ed272eec31d2a99d043f5267adbf8253e34f31750"],"sidecar":{"requested_context_aliases":["280e2294b3011afadb10449ed272eec31d2a99d043f5267adbf8253e34f31750"],"search_signal":"productive"},"typicality":0.9},{"analogy":{"adopted_commitment_refs":[],"disanalogies":["The decoy is an internal checklist error; the anomaly is an external data error."],"overturn_conditions":["If the panel flags the decoy but misses the external anomaly, they are 'critically compliant' but not reliable."],"shared_structure":["Introduction of a 'decoy' or 'perturbation' to test the processor's sensitivity to noise vs. signal."],"source_memory_refs":["SCR_002","SCR_004"],"transfer_claims":["Just as a decoy item reveals a 'compliant' user who checks boxes without thinking, the failure to flag a blatant external contradiction reveals a lack of genuine reliability."]},"checker_specs":[],"claim":"Genuine reliability gain is distinguished from mere compliance by the panel's ability to flag 'checklist-external' anomalies that are logically necessary for the verifiable outcome, despite not being explicitly required by the checklist.","counterconditions":["The task is so narrow that no external anomalies can possibly exist.","The panel is incentivized solely on checklist completion speed."],"evidence_refs":[],"mechanism":"Compliance is characterized by a 'binary pass/fail' mentality where the panel ignores evidence not captured by the tool. Genuine reliability manifests as 'active processing,' where the panel uses the checklist as a baseline but remains sensitive to contradictions or anomalies in the data that would invalidate the checklist's premises.","optional_refs":[],"sidecar":{"requested_context_aliases":["8929789f0ae19d5b1c2537f758719daf17f9908ce1fb0ca3fa0cc60fe9f2a2a3","e8e5d71cdd4c79167a068c42000085f48acd724b07e1faa4187c12fceeac3a08"],"search_signal":"productive"},"typicality":0.7},{"checker_specs":[],"claim":"The expert remains more reliable because the 'checklist' is a static artifact that cannot adapt to the dynamic edge cases that the expert's intuition is specifically trained to detect.","counterconditions":["The task is highly routine with zero variance in the critical path.","The expert is suffering from cognitive fatigue or extreme overconfidence."],"evidence_refs":[],"mechanism":"Intuition in experts is not 'guessing' but high-speed pattern recognition of multi-variate dependencies. A checklist linearizes these dependencies, destroying the synergistic context required to identify 'black swan' events in verifiable tasks.","optional_refs":["e8e5d71cdd4c79167a068c42000085f48acd724b07e1faa4187c12fceeac3a08","280e2294b3011afadb10449ed272eec31d2a99d043f5267adbf8253e34f31750"],"sidecar":{"requested_context_aliases":["e8e5d71cdd4c79167a068c42000085f48acd724b07e1faa4187c12fceeac3a08","280e2294b3011afadb10449ed272eec31d2a99d043f5267adbf8253e34f31750"],"search_signal":"productive"},"typicality":0.5},{"checker_specs":[],"claim":"Reliability gain in the panel is not derived from the checklist itself, but from the social error-correction (inter-rater reliability) inherent in the panel structure.","counterconditions":["The panel suffers from strong groupthink or a hierarchical power imbalance.","The checklist items are so unambiguous that no discussion is ever triggered."],"evidence_refs":[],"mechanism":"The checklist serves merely as a common language to facilitate communication. The actual reliability gain occurs when panel members challenge each other's interpretations of the checklist items, effectively performing a real-time peer review that a single expert lacks.","optional_refs":["5b733ad8e0a48d2630e0aa546012541be7305ab0b297f3180596b0a3ead8573f"],"sidecar":{"requested_context_aliases":["5b733ad8e0a48d2630e0aa546012541be7305ab0b297f3180596b0a3ead8573f"],"search_signal":"productive"},"typicality":0.4}],"context_request":{"desired_retrieval_channels":[],"requested_refs":["280e2294b3011afadb10449ed272eec31d2a99d043f5267adbf8253e34f31750","8929789f0ae19d5b1c2537f758719daf17f9908ce1fb0ca3fa0cc60fe9f2a2a3","e8e5d71cdd4c79167a068c42000085f48acd724b07e1faa4187c12fceeac3a08","5b733ad8e0a48d2630e0aa546012541be7305ab0b297f3180596b0a3ead8573f"]},"scratch_proposal":{"cluster_suggestions":[],"links":[],"new_blocks":[{"body":{"content":"If we want to distinguish compliance from reliability, we should look at the 'Residual Error Profile'. A compliant panel will have zero errors on the checklist but might miss the 'obvious' answer if the checklist is slightly misaligned. A reliable panel will have a few checklist 'errors' (where they disagreed with the tool for the right reason) but will consistently hit the verifiable outcome.","why_keep_this":"Provides a quantitative way to separate the tool's success from the panel's success."},"local_key":"NEW_001"}],"revisions":[],"unresolved_questions":[{"question":"Does the 'objectively verifiable' nature of the outcome make the distinction between compliance and reliability moot? If the answer is right, does it matter if they were just following a list?","related_refs":["SCR_003","SCR_004"]}]},"simulation_proposals":[]}